      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 91. An annual: it is sown or bought as a young plant after the last frost and ends with the first frost (NC State, Missouri BG; RHS: half-hardy annual, plant out in early June in the south of England). Stored as lifecycle annual. Sources: NC State and Missouri BG (both USDA-based), RHS growing guide for the UK timing, ASPCA genus page (Zinnia species, non-toxic to dogs and cats; NC State tags it non-toxic for cats, dogs and horses). Size: NC State 6 in to 3 ft by 8 in to 1 ft, Missouri BG up to 4 ft; 90 by 30 cm is the agent's mapping. Watering: Missouri BG evenly moist and well-drained, NC State occasionally dry; let_top_dry is a mapping and 3 days a guess. No hardiness stored (annual). People: no source states a grade, so no child or adult line. Es and it names are machine drafts; no es or it care page read."
      },
